title DAHL-J10r1 — skate_group, admission by quorum, never one hand
prompt continue the 1,024-round itinerary Lindy-first crux-first; take the next agent-doable lap, approve own design rounds, send each finished increment as its own signed round, stop at custody gates
think Read REMEMBER + the 1,024-round itinerary. Seasons 1 (TACT) and 2 (Yield) stand complete; Season 3 (Commons, DAHL) Journey 9 (Skate) just closed end to end (git nib 742a8573fc). No custody gate blocks — the next Lindy-first crux on the whole road is DAHL Journey 10 (Membership), the quorum surface the itinerary names, extending settlement/names.rye.
think Read settlement/names.rye and skate_circle.rye (J9r1) for the idioms. names.rye's own header says it plainly: names are the one surface that genuinely needs consensus. J9 proved consent at its smallest size — exactly-two mutual link. J10's durable new law is the next size up: threshold-of-n quorum, proven at more than two keepers. That distinction is the crux and it is Lindy-durable — the quorum rule is read for as long as the commons lives.
think Design decision: a Group opens with a founder roster and a fixed quorum t (2 <= t <= roster). A member votes for a candidate; the candidate is seated only when t DISTINCT members have voted. The honesty is distinctness with threshold — one keeper voting twice is counted once (AlreadyVoted), so a lone steward can never manufacture a quorum. Admission is derived from the distinct-vote count reaching t (no direct add-member), mirroring how J9 derived a link from two opposing requests rather than storing it. is_member follows the verdict exactly (invariant-asserted).
think Ordering care in vote(): if this vote would reach quorum and the roster is full, refuse GroupFull BEFORE recording the vote, so the bound holds before consent is counted rather than counting consent the group cannot honor.
think Self-approved the design round (exploration doc), then wrote pond/apps/skate_group.rye + tools/dahl_j10_skate_group_witness.rish. Witness GREEN first run (2 welcomes: quorum-of-two admits, quorum-of-three needs three; 4 refusals: double-vote-cannot-fake-quorum, non-member/re-admit, bad openings, full roster).
obs tame_style_check caught one compound assert (open() postcondition asserting quorum >= 2 and quorum <= member_count) — split into two named asserts per the TAME ban, exactly the discipline. Re-ran: TAME bans clean, width-check clean, witness re-GREEN.
obs The quorum-of-three test is the honest heart of the journey — consent proven past two keepers, where J9's number-two rule could not reach. The double-vote-refuses-and-tally-holds test is the load-bearing safety property: one hand can never count for two.
loom witness=dahl_j10_skate_group_witness cases=6 members_bound=32 votes_bound=256 result=GREEN
